===Etymology===
{{dercat|en|gmh|goh|orv|ine-bsl-pro|sla|ira}}
{{bor+|en|de|Hamster}} (see for etymology). Displaced earlier term {{m|en|German rat}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈhæm(p)stɚ/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-uk-hamster.ogg|a=UK}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of various Old-World rodent species belonging to the subfamily {{taxfmt|Cricetinae|subfamily}}.
## especially of species {{taxfmt|Mesocricetus auratus|species}} (the [[golden hamster]]) and species of genus {{taxfmt|Phodopus|genus}} ({{vern|dwarf hamster|pl=s}}), often kept as a [[pet]] or used in scientific research.
##: {{ux|en|The '''hamster''' stuffed his puffy cheeks with food.}}
# Other rodents of similar appearance, such as the maned hamster or crested hamster, {{taxlink|Lophiomys imhausi|species}}, mouse-like hamsters of genus {{taxlink|Calomyscus|genus}}, and the white-tailed rat ({{taxlink|Mystromys albicaudatus|species}}).

